# Microsoft Entra ID (Azure AD) configuration for HFS FHIR Server
#
# This file documents the environment variables needed to connect HFS to Entra ID
# for both SMART Backend Services (machine-to-machine) and the browser UI (SMART App Launch).
#
# Setup steps:
#   1. Register the HFS API application (Entra ID → App registrations → New registration)
#      - Name: HFS FHIR API
#      - Supported account types: Single tenant (or multi-tenant as appropriate)
#      - Note the Application (client) ID → ENTRA_API_CLIENT_ID
#      - Note the Directory (tenant) ID → ENTRA_TENANT_ID
#      - Under "Expose an API":
#          Set Application ID URI (e.g., api://<ENTRA_API_CLIENT_ID>)
#          Add scopes for SMART operations:
#            system/.default, user.cruds, user.read, patient.read
#          Note: Entra scope names cannot contain '/' or '*' characters, so use
#          dot-separated equivalents and map them to SMART format in a claims policy.
#
#   2. Map Entra app roles to SMART scopes
#      Under "App roles" (on the HFS FHIR API registration), add:
#        - fhir-admin    → maps to user/*.cruds in token claim transformation
#        - fhir-reader   → maps to user/*.rs
#        - fhir-patient  → maps to patient/Patient.r patient/Observation.rs
#
#      Then add a "claims mapping policy" or use optional claims to inject the
#      SMART scope strings into the access token's "roles" or a custom claim.
#      Use a custom claims mapping policy to transform role names to SMART scope strings
#      in the "scp" or a custom claim that HFS reads (HFS_AUTH_TENANT_CLAIM can be adjusted).
#
#      Alternatively, configure SMART scope strings directly as app role values
#      (e.g., value: "user/*.cruds") — Entra will include these in the "roles" array.
#
#   3. Register the backend service application (for client_credentials)
#      (Entra ID → App registrations → New registration)
#      - Name: HFS Backend Service
#      - Under "Certificates & secrets": create a client secret → ENTRA_CLIENT_SECRET
#      - Under "API permissions": add the HFS FHIR API app roles needed
#      - Grant admin consent for the directory
#
#   4. Register the browser UI application (SPA)
#      (Entra ID → App registrations → New registration)
#      - Name: HFS FHIR UI
#      - Redirect URI: Select "Single-page application (SPA)"
#        Add: http://localhost:5173/callback
#      - PKCE is automatically required for SPA registrations — no client secret
#      - Under "API permissions": add the HFS FHIR API delegated scopes
#      - Set UI_ENTRA_CLIENT_ID from this registration's Application (client) ID
#
# For more details see: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity-platform/v2-oauth2-auth-code-flow

# ── Shared ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
ENTRA_TENANT_ID=<directory tenant id, e.g. xxxxxxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxxxxxxxxxx>
ENTRA_API_CLIENT_ID=<HFS FHIR API app registration client id>

# ── Backend Services (client_credentials flow) ──────────────────────────────
ENTRA_CLIENT_ID=<backend service app registration client id>
ENTRA_CLIENT_SECRET=<backend service app client secret>
# Scope for client_credentials: must be {API_CLIENT_ID}/.default
ENTRA_SCOPE=api://${ENTRA_API_CLIENT_ID}/.default

# ── Browser UI (authorization_code + PKCE) ───────────────────────────────────
# Client ID of the SPA registration — no secret for public clients
UI_ENTRA_CLIENT_ID=<spa app registration client id>

# ── HFS Server environment variables ─────────────────────────────────────────
HFS_AUTH_ENABLED=true
HFS_AUTH_JWKS_URL=https://login.microsoftonline.com/${ENTRA_TENANT_ID}/discovery/v2.0/keys
HFS_AUTH_ISSUER=https://login.microsoftonline.com/${ENTRA_TENANT_ID}/v2.0
# Audience for Entra tokens is the API's Application (client) ID
HFS_AUTH_AUDIENCE=api://${ENTRA_API_CLIENT_ID}

# SMART discovery endpoints (shown in /.well-known/smart-configuration)
HFS_SMART_AUTHORIZE_ENDPOINT=https://login.microsoftonline.com/${ENTRA_TENANT_ID}/oauth2/v2.0/authorize
HFS_SMART_TOKEN_ENDPOINT=https://login.microsoftonline.com/${ENTRA_TENANT_ID}/oauth2/v2.0/token
HFS_SMART_JWKS_URL=https://login.microsoftonline.com/${ENTRA_TENANT_ID}/discovery/v2.0/keys

# Allow the UI origin (adjust for production)
HFS_CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173
